There’s no official government figure on this, but the consensus among the scientific community is that there is no credible evidence linking vaccines to autism. The vaccine schedule relies on developmental milestones that are well-documented, and the data shows no statistical spike in neurodevelopmental disorders following childhood immunization. We’re relying on decades of peer-reviewed studies over a single decade of real-world data.

If you’re concerned about your own kid’s dosage or your own vulnerabilities to misinformation, I’d recommend checking the specific manufacturer’s data page rather than searching for conspiracy theories.

